@namespace PgmStudio.Client.Components

@* A "?" standing where a paragraph of explanation used to stand, with that paragraph behind it. Prose that
   sits open under the control it explains is restated once per copy of that control — a stack of three
   voronoi layers said what a voronoi is three times over, and pushed the knobs off the bottom of the panel.
   The words are unchanged; they are one click away.

   A native <details>, so there is no script and no state to keep, and the body flows in place rather than
   floating — a popover in a scrolling panel is clipped by it. Every note shares one `name`, which makes the
   group exclusive: opening one closes the last, so the panel never fills up with open explanations. *@

<details class="help-note" name="studio-help">
  <summary title="@Title">?</summary>
  <div class="help-note-body">@ChildContent</div>
</details>

@code {
    /// <summary>The hover title on the "?" — what the note is about, in a few words.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Title { get; set; } = "What this is";

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
